                "sweepMetres": "The blade sculls just ahead of her bow, about 0.3 m beyond her 0.69 m half-width: 1 m from her middle",
                "pole": "Poled standing amidships: her 1.07 m of beam bears a man standing about as stiffly as a canoe polers stand in, stiffer than the narrowest of them (bin/lib/hulls/physics.py). No source shows a coracle poled; a man stands in the middle of her, the one place that keeps her level. His hands end the shove at his hip, 0.93 m over his soles (0.530 of a 1.756 m stature: Drillis & Contini 1966; ANSUR II, Gordon et al. 2014); his eyes at vanilla's standing 1.7 m",
                "bowDrag": "Round, so the same from every side as across her",
                "sideDrag": "A short upright cylinder in cross-flow, mirrored at the surface into one twice her draft, has a drag coefficient of about 0.6 on diameter by height (Hoerner 1965, Fluid-Dynamic Drag, ch. 3); a bowl's rounded bottom sheds less, as a sphere's 0.47 on its frontal area does"
