            "damage": {"material": "hide"},
            "sources": {
                "parts": "By the model (bin/lib/hulls/coracle.py): 2.18 m² of hide 5 mm thick at 860 kg/m³, 9.4 kg, over 14 lattice laths and three plaits of 1 by 6 cm, 32 m of willow, 8 kg: 17 kg, as Hornell (1938) gives one-man coracles at 18 to 40 lb",
                "shell": "Raw cowhide is 2 to 6 mm thick. A blow springs back off the hide unless a lath backs it where it lands: by the model, the lattice's 14 laths 6 cm wide cross 65% of the bottom, and their 28 ends rising to the gunwale 47% of the sides. A breaker presses the hide onto them, each lath 1 cm deep bending over the 0.37 m from the bottom to the gunwale. A knock, a ram or rapids presses the hide onto the lath behind where it lands: wet hide stretches to 60% before it parts (pickled cowhide, 26.6 MPa at 60% elongation; Tensile Properties of Indigenous Kenyan Boran Pickled and Tanned Bovine Hide), so on a lath it passes the blow on, and the lath, 1 by 6 cm of willow, breaks by its impact bending work across its section; between two laths, their 6 cm breadth over 47% of her sides setting them 12.8 cm apart and crossing as far, it sags as a membrane until its pull breaks both. Hornell (British Coracles and Irish Curraghs, 1938) has coracles shoot rapids on rock-strewn rivers and a hole or a rent mended with a tarred patch",
                "runsRapids": "She shoots them as the bark canoe does: Hornell (British Coracles and Irish Curraghs, 1938) has her float in from 2 to 3 in. of water, go almost anywhere and shoot rapids and thread narrow channels. A stub, as the rapids' strike is (rapids.json): until rapids are worked out from draft (#260), which hull runs them is this flag",
                "seep": "A seam where one hide meets the next weeps once the fat has washed out of it: some 1.8 m of seam across her bowl, weeping as the currach's do a metre. A coracle from before her build is covered in prepared hide over her two sections, with no seam, as her old recipe's one large hide had",
                "cover": "The hides a vessel is covered with as her build lays them; one from before her build is covered with prepared hides, as the grid made her"
            },
